{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of scale, siting, design, bulk, mass and appearance would be an undesirable addition,&amp;nbsp;representing an overly dominant and excessive addition to the semi-detaching dwelling. The rear extension would be significantly visible from public vantage points and would be visually intrusive, represent poor design and would be out of character in the context of the area, specifically within the Becontree Estate. In particular, the proposal would not sit comfortably within the existing pattern of development.&amp;nbsp; The accumulative impact of the first floor rear extension and existing extensions would result in the creation of a significantly developed and staggered roof form.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;As such, the proposal would cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and surrounding area and is&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;harmful to the appearance of the semi-detached dwelling&amp;nbsp; and character of the area, notably given the location of the application site within the Becontree Estate. As such, the proposed development is contrary to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;. The proposal is therefore contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development recognises local character and promotes good design:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt; - National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)- The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037: (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
